    basic: "Remember what other people ask for. If Tom asks Sarah for the Jack of Spades and Sarah doesn't have it, you now know Tom has a Jack and Sarah does not have the Jack of Spades.",
    intermediate: "The Bluff: If you hold three Kings and need the fourth, ask someone who you know DOESN'T have it to end your turn, making others think you are weak on Kings. (Risky, as someone might target you next).",
    advanced: 'Elimination Mapping: Mentally track every revealed suit of a rank. If you see the Jack of Spades and Jack of Hearts go to one player, and you hold the Jack of Clubs, you only need to find the Jack of Diamonds to swoop the whole set.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Pay attention even when it's not your turn. The information revealed during other people's turns is essential for winning.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Collect 'quietly'. Don't ask for the same rank three times in a row unless you are sure you can complete the book on that turn.",
      },
